<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese state firm takes Efacec stake.</title>
<headline>Portuguese state firm takes Efacec stake.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering concern Efacec said in a statement that  IPE-Investimento &amp; Participacoes, a state investment company, had bought a 10 percent stake in the company.  </p>
<p>The company gave no further information.</p>
<p>Efacec shares closed down 23 escudos at 1,437 escudos on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 10 percent stake would involve the purchase of some 750,000 shares.</p>
<p>($1=163.51 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
